review.verdict:
Mostly sound; acceptable after one documentation fix and some minor hardening. I diffed the two listed source files against their snapshots, read baseline.md, ran src/dev/xrayCapture.test.ts (9 passed) and npx tsc -p tsconfig.app.json --noEmit (clean), and reran compare_sets.py for baseline vs baseline (no lost, no gained) and baseline vs narrow-left (178/236, rows lost as reported). The stored scorecard_matched.json has 248 rows, 189/236 passing, and 6 measurement runs with 462 rows, all pass None and none in rows. dev_guide's frame hashes equal lad_raocra's. The live metadata confirms that the PCI lab ran in real time (1280 px) and the diagnostic lab was stepped (988 px, JL4 seated in the LM, injection made).

Every acceptance criterion is met. The device scenes are driven through the real PCI engine and drawn by the lab's own pciDevices and pciFlowMods. The live path films both labs through their own render paths. report.py keeps device and live rows out of the headline, and compare_sets.py reads only rows. No file under src/render/ changed, and the scorecard specs and default paths are unchanged (prepareScenario with no options gives the same scene). The file under scripts/ changed after .started (scripts/README.md) belongs to found-launch-links, and every other src/ file changed since .started belongs to the lab-tips and content packages.

There are no unsourced clinical numbers. Device sizes come from the scenario geometry and the pressures from the engine catalogue's own BALLOON_SPEC and STENT_SPEC, and the 2-row tolerance is in the plan, section 2. Tip integration, lesson and case links, design system and ground truth do not apply. There is no per-frame allocation in any lab render path; the render tap exists only during a capture.

The main gap: the design requires the row list in docs/realism/baseline.md, but it lives only in datasets/tmp. The minor items:
- the render tap drops the target argument of XrayRenderer.render;
- the live path no longer checks that the lab canvas is square, and films a frozen PCI clock without complaint;
- one narrowed-tree assertion is tautological;
- report.py's role split has no automated test;
- the 16 mm device length is not one the lab offers;
- live capture changes the open case without saying so;
- the baseline device states depend on a test helper.
